 "status": "TANGENT VELOCITIES AND NODE LITTLE GROUPS (O9). T1: measured exactly, not at a finite radius, the 12 V63 doubler nodes have tangent speeds along the three axes (0.00000, 0.14189, 0.14189) - one axis direction is exactly flat, the other two carry equal speeds; V115's finite-difference velocities converge as dq -> 0 (exponent 0.00 on a linear branch, -1.00 on the flat one, i.e. a quadratic gap), so the anisotropy is NOT a dq = 1e-3 artifact. T2: the nodes sit at zone-EDGE momenta whose little group is C2v - two equal velocities and a free third, exactly what is measured - while the supercell zone CORNER (pi/2,pi/2,pi/2) carries exactly 3-fold degenerate multiplets (splitting < 1e-12): the full octahedral group is realised there. T3: the V65 Wilson factor drives a corner cubic TRIPLET exactly gapless (gap 1.2e-10 and 7.1e-11 at independent (theta,w) points) - the first exactly massless cubic multiplet found in the model, a one-parameter family. T4: on that subspace dM/dq_j is anti-hermitian (err 1.4e-10) and the velocity operators S_j = i dM/dq_j are nonzero (max speed 0.922 in lattice units): the touching IS linear, not quadratic. T4b: but the three velocity operators COMMUTE (max ||[S_i,S_j]|| = 3.2e-12) and sum_j S_j^2 is a scalar - the three branches carry three FIXED velocity vectors, so the node is a crossing of three NODAL PLANES, not a cone: the 6588 branch-directions span [1.5e-03, 0.922], 36 of them are exactly gapless, and every branch speed equals |v_alpha . d| to 5.5e-12 - the node is three planes. VERDICT: the failure of continuous Lorentz invariance is structural, not a tuning failure. A cone requires the tangent velocity operators to close a Clifford-type algebra; in the implemented step they commute, because the bond layer is a Kronecker product (cell index) x (internal algebra) and never mixes the two. Closing O9 requires a bond layer that entangles the cell and internal indices."
